The first equation of the double fixed point holds: fTok of Gamma_D and Gamma_E equals Gamma_D.

A token of fTok of the two colimits lies, by single-stage additivity, in fTok of some stage, hence in the next first component of the iteration and so in Gamma_D. A token of Gamma_D lies at some stage. The zeroth stage is the empty string, which belongs to fTok. A later stage lies in fTok of the preceding components, and those components sit inside the colimits, so monotonicity places the token in fTok of the colimits.
